name 'ai-powered-threats-defenses-lesson10-level1_2025-pilot_v3'
title 'AI in Encryption'

question 'Which explanation best describes how an AI password-guessing system creates its predictions?'

wrong 'It guesses randomly until it finds a password that works.'
right 'It uses personal data and leaked password patterns to predict likely choices.'
wrong 'It can read your private messages to learn your password.'
wrong 'It already knows everyone\'s passwords from its training data. '
allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
AI tools trained on large datasets recognize patterns in how people create passwords. They do not read private content or “know” anyone’s password; they predict likely choices based on common patterns.
MARKDOWN
